---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const interpretComplaintResult = await interpretComplaint(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const linkRelatedIssuesResult = await linkRelatedIssues(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, interpretComplaintResult.accepted);
const formWorkOrdersResult = await formWorkOrders(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, linkRelatedIssuesResult.accepted);
const coordinateVisitsResult = await coordinateVisits(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, formWorkOrdersResult.accepted);
const verifyResolutionResult = await verifyResolution(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, coordinateVisitsResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { interpretComplaint: interpretComplaintResult, linkRelatedIssues: linkRelatedIssuesResult, formWorkOrders: formWorkOrdersResult, coordinateVisits: coordinateVisitsResult, verifyResolution: verifyResolutionResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...interpretComplaintResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...linkRelatedIssuesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...formWorkOrdersResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...coordinateVisitsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...verifyResolutionResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...interpretComplaintResult.checks, ...linkRelatedIssuesResult.checks, ...formWorkOrdersResult.checks, ...coordinateVisitsResult.checks, ...verifyResolutionResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A room has an informal name: maintain aliases without changing the official asset location. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (maintain aliases without changing the official asset location.) through the existing stage result for FacilityObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior FacilityObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A technician cannot gain access: record the failed visit and renegotiate consented access. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (record the failed visit and renegotiate consented access.) through the existing stage result for FacilityObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior FacilityObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — Noise occurs only at certain times: schedule observation under the relevant conditions. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (schedule observation under the relevant conditions.) through the existing stage result for FacilityObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior FacilityObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — Several occupants report one issue: send privacy-preserving updates without exposing identities. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (send privacy-preserving updates without exposing identities.) through the existing stage result for FacilityObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior FacilityObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A repair recurs repeatedly: escalate the mechanism investigation rather than opening disconnected tickets. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (escalate the mechanism investigation rather than opening disconnected tickets.) through the existing stage result for FacilityObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior FacilityObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, interpretComplaint: interpretComplaintResult, linkRelatedIssues: linkRelatedIssuesResult, formWorkOrders: formWorkOrdersResult, coordinateVisits: coordinateVisitsResult, verifyResolution: verifyResolutionResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
